<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-QA-119>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-QA-119" ;
  triage:title "Intermittent failure of atm_temp not_writable_io_error_is_logged_not_discarded (tracing-capture race)" ;
  triage:description "rust-qa-agent's full `cargo test --workspace` failed atm_temp::tests::unix_only::not_writable_io_error_is_logged_not_discarded (crates/atm-core/src/atm_temp.rs:580 at the integrate head) in 1 of 2 full-workspace runs while 4 isolated agent-team-mail-core runs passed 583/583. Suspected cause: a race in the tracing-capture helper in crates/atm-core/src/test_support.rs (global tracing subscriber shared across concurrently running tests, so a capture can miss or receive another test's events). The capture_tracing function uses a process-global subscriber installed via set_global_default at line 287, with per-thread buffers keyed by ThreadId. In cargo test parallelism, two concurrent tests on the same thread (or thread reuse by the test harness) can interleave: the first test's capture_tracing call removes its buffer at line 296, runs the test, and collects logs; but if the thread is reused or events from other tests fire between removal and collection, the capture can miss events or receive another test's tracing output. Unrelated to PR #1255's diff; pre-existing. Per the no-flaky-tolerance rule this needs a root cause and a deterministic fix (e.g. per-test subscriber scoping with tracing::subscriber::with_default, or serializing the tests that install a global capture), not a rerun. Remediation must make the test deterministic under `cargo test --workspace` parallelism and must not weaken the assertion. The helper is capture_tracing at crates/atm-core/src/test_support.rs:210, which delegates to tracing_capture::capture; the actual race is in ensure_installed at line 280-288 where set_global_default is called exactly once via std::sync::Once, installing GlobalCaptureProxy. The fix should either use with_default per-scope (accepting the known with_default cache-rebuild cost documented in the comment at lines 188-205) and testing it does not regress with concurrent loads, or implement true per-test subscriber isolation." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
